---
import Section from './Section.astro';
import Eyebrow from './Eyebrow.astro';
import RoleDiagram from './RoleDiagram.astro';
---

<Section id="structural-problem">
  <Eyebrow class="reveal">The structural problem</Eyebrow>

  <h2 class="h2 reveal" style="--reveal-delay:60ms">Every vendor grades its own homework.</h2>

  <div class="reveal mt-10" style="--reveal-delay:120ms">
    <RoleDiagram />
  </div>

  <div class="mt-12 grid grid-cols-1 gap-10 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1.35fr)_minmax(0,1fr)] lg:gap-16">
    <p class="reveal body">
      Aardvark writes the patch with Codex, then scans its own patch. CodeMender, Snyk,
      Pixee, Mobb and ZeroPath all certify their own work. Google still puts a human
      researcher on every CodeMender patch before it ships: the best resourced team on
      earth does not trust its own fixer.
    </p>

    <div class="reveal border-t border-line pt-6 lg:border-l lg:border-t-0 lg:pl-8 lg:pt-0" style="--reveal-delay:60ms">
      <p class="hd mb-4">Second beat</p>
      <p class="body text-fg-2">
        The human backstop broke too. Developers using AI ship three to four times more
        code. Review capacity did not.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  {/* The conclusion the diagram and the vendor list both arrive at, standing
      on its own rather than trailing the paragraph. */}
  <p class="statement reveal mt-14" style="--reveal-delay:60ms">
    Independence is the one thing <span class="q">an author can never sell you.</span>
  </p>
</Section>
